│                          │ random initialization with `rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=42)`). This edit replaces    │
│                          │ that naive random initialization with a deterministic multi-start optimizer: several      │
│                          │ candidate layouts (3-fold symmetric rings, a triangular-lattice pattern, Sobol            │
│                          │ quasi-random with fixed seed, and one random restart), each refined by a multi-stage      │
│                          │ stochastic hill-climb that directly maximizes the minimum triangle area normalized by the │
│                          │ convex hull area (scale-invariant objective). The final configuration is rescaled so its  │
│                          │ convex hull has unit area, matching the problem's unit-area normalization. All operations │
│                          │ are seeded, so results are deterministic and reproducible.                                │
