│ patch_name               │ annealed_multistart_heilbronn13                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver as a staged pipeline (candidate generation → simulated annealing   │
│                          │ refinement → selection/validation) instead of per-seed hill climbing. Key improvements:   │
│                          │ (1) simulated annealing with adaptive temperature accepts occasional worsening moves to   │
│                          │ escape local optima; (2) smarter move set — simultaneous perturbation of the vertex of    │
│                          │ the current smallest triangle plus random points, since only triangles involving the      │
│                          │ bottleneck vertex matter; (3) more diverse seeds including ring+center and two-ring       │
│                          │ configurations known to help at n=13; (4) early score computation via a single vectorized │
│                          │ min-triangle routine and hull area cached per candidate. This raises min_area_normalized  │
│                          │ while keeping the run under ~2 seconds and fully deterministic (fixed seed, time-bounded  │
│                          │ but seeded so results are reproducible).                                                  │
