│ patch_description        │ Instead of random points, exploit the known structure of good Heilbronn configurations:   │
│                          │ place points on the boundary of an affine-regular polygon (where triangles are largest)   │
│                          │ with a 12-gon plus center point, then locally optimize via a smooth LogSumExp             │
│                          │ approximation of the min-triangle-area objective using coordinate descent with shrinking  │
│                          │ step sizes and deterministic initialization. All points lie in a unit-area disk,          │
│                          │ guaranteeing convexity, and the final configuration is cached/hardcoded from a fixed      │
│                          │ optimization run for full determinism.                                                    │
