│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_annealing_and_seeds                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The key weakness is the blind hill-climbing: it perturbs random points and immediately    │
│                          │ accepts any score increase, which gets stuck easily. Improvement strategy based on        │
│                          │ Heilbronn-specific geometric insight: the objective is governed by a few "bottleneck"     │
│                          │ triangles, so moves should target vertices of the currently-smallest triangles. I also    │
│                          │ improve seeds (12-gon + center, two-ring 7+6 configuration are classic boundary-heavy     │
│                          │ Heilbronn candidates), use simulated annealing with reheating to escape local optima,     │
│                          │ always track the global best, and use a scale-invariant step size (sigma scaled by hull   │
│                          │ diameter) so moves don't stall for small/large configurations. Targeted edits to the seed │
│                          │ construction and the optimization loop.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
