│                          │ body with a deterministic hybrid optimizer for the 13-point Heilbronn triangle problem:   │
│                          │ multi-start initialization (3-fold symmetric ring configurations and seeded uniform       │
│                          │ random starts), targeted local search that moves the vertices of the globally smallest    │
│                          │ triangle along its area gradient with line search and re-targeting on stalls, followed by │
│                          │ a softmin (LogSumExp) polish over all near-minimal triangles. Points are confined to the  │
│                          │ unit square (unit area, convex). Only moves that strictly improve the true minimum        │
│                          │ triangle area are accepted, and fixed seeds/iteration counts guarantee reproducibility.   │
