│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ softmin_adam_multistart_h13                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ All prior programs plateau at ~0.02 normalized min-area, and all rely on single-point     │
│                          │ stochastic perturbation or per-parameter numeric gradients — too weak to coordinate all   │
│                          │ 26 coordinates jointly. The key insight exploited here: the score is scale-invariant, so  │
│                          │ if we rescale the configuration to unit hull area each step, the score equals the raw     │
│                          │ minimum triangle area, and we can directly ascend a smooth soft-min (LogSumExp) surrogate │
│                          │ of the minimum triangle area using exact analytic gradients over all 26 coordinates       │
│                          │ simultaneously (Adam). Per-triangle area gradients ∂area/∂A,∂B,∂C are computed vectorized │
│                          │ and aggregated with softmax weights w_t ∝ exp(-p·a_t); the sharpening parameter p anneals │
│                          │ so the surrogate converges to the true min. Each step rescales points to unit hull area,  │
│                          │ making the smooth objective a faithful proxy of the true score. Eight diverse structured  │
│                          │ seeds (13-gon, ellipse, two-arc clusters, superellipse rounded square, spiral, double     │
│                          │ ring, 12-ring+center, perturbed polygon) — all valid by construction — are optimized      │
│                          │ under a deterministic time budget, followed by an exact hill-climb polish with            │
│                          │ bottleneck-triangle-directed moves. Exact score bookkeeping guarantees we never return    │
│                          │ worse than any visited configuration, and a fallback regular 13-gon covers any failure.   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0305                                                                                   │
