│ patch_description        │ History shows Gen 19's strict-acceptance hill climb with 50% bottleneck-vertex-targeted   │
│                          │ moves (0.60 → 0.63) beat both full bottleneck-only targeting (Gen 13–18) and the directed │
│                          │ perpendicular-push variants. The current `_polish` uses 75% directed perpendicular moves, │
│                          │ which are the historically underperforming family. Replace it with a plain 50/50 mix:     │
│                          │ with probability 0.5 perturb a randomly chosen vertex of the current minimum-area         │
│                          │ triangle (found via argmin over the 286 cross products) with a Gaussian step; otherwise   │
│                          │ perturb a uniformly random vertex. Keep strict improvement acceptance and the adaptive    │
│                          │ sigma schedule (grow on improvement, shrink otherwise). This should strictly dominate the │
│                          │ previous best structure while retaining the multi-seed + Adam pre-optimization + restart  │
│                          │ framework of the current program.                                                         │
