│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ heilbronn13_targeted_hillclimb                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the current hill-climb optimizer with the simple seeded constructor. The new │
│                          │ version retains the multi-seed + adaptive hill-climb framework but adds: (1) a targeted   │
│                          │ "vertex push" move that displaces the vertex of the current bottleneck triangle directly  │
│                          │ away from the centroid of the other two bottleneck vertices (the direction that most      │
│                          │ directly increases that triangle's area), (2) precomputed triangle index arrays and a     │
│                          │ faster area kernel, (3) a slightly expanded seed set including known-good Heilbronn-style │
│                          │ configurations (concentric rings, perturbed polygons), and (4) time-budgeted restarts     │
│                          │ with decaying sigma. The targeted move dramatically improves convergence speed on         │
│                          │ bottleneck triangles compared to blind Gaussian perturbation, raising min_area_normalized │
│                          │ within the same ~3s budget.                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
