│ patch_name               │ incremental_bottleneck_descent                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of the previous program's full 286-triangle rescore every iteration, this version │
│                          │ exploits the key geometric insight: moving a single point only changes the 66 triangles   │
│                          │ containing it. It maintains a cached full area vector and updates only the affected       │
│                          │ entries on acceptance, recomputing hull area only when a hull vertex moves (else cached). │
│                          │ This ~5x per-iteration speedup is converted into many more local-search trials per        │
│                          │ restart. The search is a deterministic greedy bottleneck descent: identify the minimal    │
│                          │ triangle, move its vertices (or a random point) with shrinking steps, accept strict       │
│                          │ improvements in min_area/hull_area. Multiple structured restarts (13-gon ring,            │
│                          │ ring+center, two-ring, jittered disk) each get a share of the time budget, followed by    │
│                          │ fine polish. Fixed seeds guarantee reproducibility.                                       │
