                        Patch Metadata - Gen 32/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ incremental_triangle_eval_speedup                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation from the previous round is still the best lever: the current code      │
│                          │ recomputes all 286 triangle areas (via fancy indexing, ~286×3×2 array) AND runs the       │
│                          │ Python-loop monotone-chain hull for every single candidate — a huge waste. Two key        │
│                          │ insights:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Single-vertex moves**: if only vertex `v` moves, only the 66 triangles containing    │
│                          │ `v` change area. Precompute, for each vertex, the index arrays of triangles               │
│                          │ containing/not containing it. Cache the full 286-area vector; on a candidate move,        │
│                          │ evaluate only the 66 affected triangles plus a vectorized `min` over the 220 untouched    │
│                          │ cached areas.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Hull caching**: if `v` is not a hull vertex and the perturbed point stays inside the │
│                          │ cached hull polygon, the hull area is unchanged — check with a vectorized                 │
│                          │ point-in-convex-polygon cross-product test. Only recompute the (Python-loop) hull when    │
│                          │ `v` was a hull vertex or the point escapes the hull. Also, dropping `_rescale` during the │
│                          │ search (score is scale-normalized anyway) avoids needless full recomputes.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This gives roughly a 4x+ per-candidate speedup, converting directly into many more        │
│                          │ hill-climb iterations and restarts within the same time budget — the proven route to      │
│                          │ higher scores. Determinism preserved via the fixed seed and fixed time budget split.      │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0218                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ z-ai/glm-5.3                                                                              │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'low'}                                                                         │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 98; deleted: 0; modified: 39;                                                      │
