│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ soft_quantile_phase                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The pure soft-min objective collapses all gradient mass onto the single bottleneck        │
│                          │ triangle, which strands other near-degenerate triangles at the 0.02 plateau. Adding a     │
│                          │ second gradient phase that minimizes a soft τ-quantile of the 286 areas (τ ≈ 0.05–0.10)   │
│                          │ spreads gradient weight across the whole weak tail, matching the true "maximize the       │
│                          │ minimum" structure better and letting the plateau break. I add a differentiable quantile  │
│                          │ surrogate via a soft indicator (sigmoid on area − threshold), take its exact gradient     │
│                          │ with respect to points, and run it as an Adam phase on the incumbent best configuration   │
│                          │ before the final polish. The surrogate uses a threshold annealed from the min area        │
│                          │ upward, so it focuses on exactly the bottom ~5–10% of triangles.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0228                                                                                   │
