                        Patch Metadata - Gen 45/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_gradient_ascent_hops                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The key insight from the prior programs: basin quality is the binding constraint, and     │
│                          │ random single-point perturbations waste most evaluations. The novel approach here         │
│                          │ replaces blind stochastic moves with *exact gradient information from the bottleneck      │
│                          │ triangle itself*: the area of the smallest triangle is a simple quadratic function of its │
│                          │ three vertices, so its gradient (perpendicular push away from the opposite edge for each  │
│                          │ vertex) is computable in closed form. I implement (1) a fast incremental evaluator that   │
│                          │ recomputes only the 66 affected triangles when a single point moves, (2) a deterministic  │
│                          │ gradient-ascent mode that simultaneously translates all three bottleneck vertices along   │
│                          │ their exact area gradients with adaptive step size (a correlated move random noise cannot │
│                          │ discover), and (3) basin-hopping kicks that, per the recommendation, perturb only 3–4     │
│                          │ vertices at σ=0.13–0.15 or rigidly translate the bottleneck triangle, followed by a quick │
│                          │ gradient-polish. Scale-invariance is handled by rescaling to unit hull area after each    │
│                          │ accepted move, keeping the score well-conditioned.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0251                                                                                   │
