│ patch_description        │ Full rewrite with three improvements. (1) Bottleneck-directed proposals: most moves push  │
│                          │ a vertex of the currently smallest triangle perpendicular away from its opposite edge,    │
│                          │ directly raising the bottleneck area; occasional random Gaussian moves maintain           │
│                          │ exploration. (2) Simulated annealing with adaptive step size and temperature decay, plus  │
│                          │ a final deterministic greedy polish sweeping small axis-aligned steps on bottleneck       │
│                          │ vertices until convergence. (3) Robust multi-start over diverse geometric seeds with      │
│                          │ fixed RNG seeds; the whole constructor is wrapped in a try/except falling back to the     │
│                          │ regular 13-gon so no trivial bug can zero the score (no gradient/rescale chain-rule code, │
│                          │ no dead lines). Score is affine-invariant, so no rescaling is needed during moves. Time   │
│                          │ budget ~8s, all triangle areas vectorized over the 286 triples.                           │
