│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tail_surrogate_and_speed_fix                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted changes based on the observed plateau (all programs stuck at min_area=0.02   │
│                          │ with combined scores 0.62–0.72, meaning the score rewards the geometry of the whole       │
│                          │ small-area tail, not just the single bottleneck triangle):                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Remove a wasteful redundant computation**: the inner loop calls                      │
│                          │ `_hull_area(points=x) - _hull_area(x)` on the same array twice — a no-op comparison that  │
│                          │ costs O(n log n) per candidate move across hundreds of thousands of iterations. Deleting  │
│                          │ it frees substantial CPU for more search iterations per seed.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Replace the pure "mean of k smallest" soft objective with a tail-weighted            │
│                          │ surrogate** `S = 0.5·min + 0.5·mean(bottom-5)`. The old soft term ignored the actual      │
│                          │ bottleneck (min), so uphill-escape moves could drift away from configurations whose       │
│                          │ bottleneck was large. The combined surrogate keeps the bottleneck heavily weighted while  │
│                          │ still smoothing over the 5 smallest triangles, so the annealing phase relaxes toward      │
│                          │ configurations where several near-degenerate triangles are simultaneously lifted —        │
│                          │ exactly the tail geometry the combined score rewards. This mirrors the recommended        │
│                          │ multi-term tail surrogate (softmin over all 286 + soft-min over the bottom-5) but         │
│                          │ implemented cheaply with `np.partition`, keeping the incremental-update machinery intact. │
