│ patch_name               │ hybrid_adam_hillclimb_refine                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The Adam/softmin approach scores 0.72, while pure hill-climbing scored 0.68. Each         │
│                          │ optimizer has complementary strengths: softmin-Adam makes coordinated global              │
│                          │ rearrangements (escaping poor basin shapes), while greedy bottleneck-pool hill-climbing   │
│                          │ makes sharp, exact max-min moves once near a local optimum (softmin with finite           │
│                          │ temperature plateaus before the true min is maximized). The edit:                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Adds structured seeds on a parabola (a classical Heilbronn test curve where triangle   │
│                          │ areas factor into products of gaps — a good basin for max-min configurations) and a       │
│                          │ stretched lattice.                                                                        │
│                          │ 2. Adds a deterministic greedy refinement routine `_refine` that perturbs only vertices   │
│                          │ belonging to the currently-smallest triangles (bottleneck pool), with geometrically       │
│                          │ decaying step size — this performs exact max-min ascent, which softmin-Adam cannot fully  │
│                          │ achieve at finite temperature.                                                            │
│                          │ 3. Rewrites Phase 2 as a hybrid loop: each iteration does a short Adam re-anneal (global  │
│                          │ reshaping) followed by a bottleneck hill-climb polish (local exact sharpening), keeping   │
│                          │ the best of both. Since the score is scale-invariant this reliably pushes the true        │
│                          │ minimum triangle up, and the final rescale to unit hull area is preserved.                │
