│ patch_description        │ The current version plateaus at 0.02 normalized min-area across all 4 boundary-biased     │
│                          │ seeds. I add: (1) three new structurally diverse seeds built directly in the valid domain │
│                          │ — a two-arc cluster configuration, a rounded-square boundary, and an Archimedean-spiral   │
│                          │ fill — to reach different optimization basins; (2) a stronger local search that perturbs  │
│                          │ two points at a time (helps break single-point move barriers typical in Heilbronn         │
│                          │ configurations where the binding triangle involves multiple points); (3) a "small-k"      │
│                          │ objective: maximize a soft-min over the bottom few triangles (softmin via -log-sum-exp),  │
│                          │ which gives smoother gradients and escapes flat plateaus of the pure min. Softmin shares  │
│                          │ the same _score argument structure so we can reuse tri_idx. All seeds are convex-valid by │
│                          │ construction (points on curves / interior), no rescaling needed.                          │
